  <div id="sutta">
  
              <h2 id="SN22.145" class="h1">Not-self<br/>
                Anattā Sutta  (SN 22:145)</h2>
<p>Near Sāvatthī. “Monks, whatever is not-self, you should abandon desire-passion there. And what is not-self?</p>
<p>“Form, monks, is not-self. You should abandon desire-passion there.</p>
<p>“Feeling is not-self. You should abandon desire-passion there.</p>
<p>“Perception is not-self. You should abandon desire-passion there.</p>
<p>“Fabrications are not-self. You should abandon desire-passion there.</p>
<p>“Consciousness is not-self. You should abandon desire-passion there.</p>
<p>“Monks, whatever is not-self, you should abandon desire-passion there.”</p>
<p class="seealso">See also: <a href="SN22_120.html" class="sutta-ref">SN 22:120–121</a></p>
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
